\CNK@Section{Code Generation and Retargetability}\CNK@Label{sect:codegen-and-retarget}

Code generations happens at every step of a compilation pipeline. It's the sole purpose of a compiler. Even interpreters emit code to an extent. When it comes to defining ``code generation'', it's a free-for-all. Emitting intermediate code, emitting final code, refining the final code, refining the intermediate code; we could go on, and on.

This section focuses on all aspects of code generation at both the interim stages and the final stages. We discuss \CNK@IndexWord{retargetability}. The ages when there existed dozens of CPU architectures is gone. A modern compiler needs to support a handful of MPU targets, as we'll see. But \CNK@IndexWord{Compute targets} are a different story.

This section implements \CNK@CaseStudy{Surtmeh} as a case study. Surtmeh is an \CNK@IndexWord{Architecture Definition Language} and it has a library that offers these.
